  "description": "ODAREU crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 4/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H116 Ce6 O32 P4,2(C5 H5 N1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2C (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1H (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.824-3.920 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 110.70-112.58°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6O4(OH)4(O2PPh2)4(O2C^tBu)8]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
